# Large or local-only files. The CAD's source STEP files are too big for GitHub (the RCC's is 101 MB) and are not needed to
# regenerate a guide (the converted .glb files are kept); their checksums are in cad-sources.sha256.
*.STEP
*.step
*.stp
*.sldprt
*.sldasm
*.SLDPRT
*.SLDASM
*.igs
*.iges
*.x_t
*.x_b
*.f3d
*.stl
*.3mf
*.dxf
# Other CAD and laser-cutting formats a new kit may bring (the cutting files are what the wood's roughening protects)
*.slddrw
*.SLDDRW
*.f3z
*.sat
*.jt
*.ipt
*.iam
*.prt
*.dwg
*.3dm
*.obj
*.fbx
*.ai
*.eps
*.cdr
*.lbrn
*.lbrn2
# The PMG's CAD export is over GitHub's 100 MB limit: the kit uses pmg-guide.glb, cut from it by make_source.py (its STEP's checksum is in cad-sources.sha256)
PMG Build Instructions/pmg.glb
# Videos, archives, phone photos (they can carry the place they were taken)
MRA_Videos/
*_Videos/
*.mov
*.MOV
*.mp4
*.m4v
*.zip
*.heic
*.HEIC
# Anything holding a key or token (a Render deploy hook, an API key), never committed
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
share/
thumbs/
# The pictures drawn for a guide's 2D PDF (player/js/pages.js -> tools/make_pdf.py): made again whenever a PDF is made
/*/pages/
# Research pictures: screenshots, the published Cadasio guides' step pictures, review contact sheets, build-video stills and
# the pictures Lee attaches in chat. Working material that stays on this Mac (Lee, 19 Oct 2026: research files need not go to
# GitHub). The notes (.md), data (.json) and scripts (.py) beside them stay in git: they are small, they are the record behind
# the rulebook, and some remake kit inputs (the Cadasio dumps behind the colour atlases and the LSM's lsm.glb). No code that
# regenerates or publishes a guide reads anything under docs/research. Pictures a guide shows live in its kit folder (parts/,
# cards/, logo.webp, an inset's picture), never here.
docs/research/**/*.jpg
docs/research/**/*.JPG
docs/research/**/*.jpeg
docs/research/**/*.png
docs/research/**/*.PNG
docs/research/**/*.webp
docs/research/**/*.gif
# A step-text sheet sent back for import (its edits are in the kit's step-text*.json once imported)
*step text*.csv
.venv.nosync/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
# The repository's own data lives in .git.nosync (kept out of iCloud sync); .git is a pointer file to it.
.git.nosync/
# publish.py's lock and unfinished copies
releases/.lock
site/.*
releases/**/.*.tmp
